px');return false">am&#8217;a</a></span> [am.ˈʔa] <em>n.</em> doubt<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/8860.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">am&#8217;ake</a></span> [am.ˈʔa.kɛ] <em>adj.</em> sure, confident<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/9068.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">am&#8217;aluke</a></span> [am.ˈʔa.lu.kɛ] <em>adv.</em> without a doubt<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13409.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">amay</a></span> [a.ˈmaj] <em>n.</em> brook<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13042.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">Amhul</a></span> [am.ˈhul] <em>prop.n.</em> female Na&#8217;vi<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/5696.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">anìheyu</a></span> [a.nɪ.ˈhɛ.ju] <em>n.</em> fibonacci, blue spiral plant<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13369.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">Anuk</a></span> [a.nʊk̚] <em>prop.n.</em> (name)<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13043.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">Anurai</a></span> [ˈa.