.ˈtɾ̣.tɾ̣] <em>n.</em> living room (on Earth)<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13063.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">Mo&#8217;ara</a></span> [mo.ˈʔa.ɾa] <em>prop.n.</em> a valley on Pandora (Note: Also the name of the Disney Pandora location)<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/11072.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">mo&#8217;ara</a></span> [mo.ˈʔa.ɾa] <em>n.</em> gathering place<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13064.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">Mo&#8217;at</a></span> [ˈmo.ʔat̚] <em>prop.n.</em> tsahìk of the Omatikaya<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13065.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">Mo&#8217;at&#8217;ite</a></span> [ˈmo.ʔat̚.ʔi.tɛ] <em>prop.n.</em> daughter of Mo&#8217;at<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/1132.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">moe</a></span> [ˈmo.ɛ] <em>pn.</em> we two, us two (exclusive)<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/6736.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">mok</a></span> [m·ok̚] <em>vtr.</em> suggest<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/1136.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,