] <em>n.</em> wife, female spouse<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/6312.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">muntxatu</a></span> [mun.ˈt&#8217;a.tu] <em>n.</em> spouse<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/5608.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">muve</a></span> [ˈmu.vɛ] <em>adj.</em> second (ordinal)<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/6740.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">muwìntxu</a></span> [mu.w·ɪn.ˈt&#8217;·u] <em>vtr.</em> introduce, present<br /></iv></div>
