> [pu.ˈp&#8217;ɪ] <em>n.</em> one-sixth<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/5624.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">puve</a></span> [ˈpu.vɛ] <em>adj.</em> sixth (ordinal)<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13401.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">puwup</a></span> [ˈp·u.w·ʊp̚] <em>vin.</em> bounce</div>
