;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13077.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">Ralu</a></span> [ˈɾa.lu] <em>prop.n.</em> male Na&#8217;vi<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/6308.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">ram</a></span> [ɾam] <em>n.</em> mountain<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/6664.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">ramtsyìp</a></span> [ˈɾam.t͡sjɪp̚] <em>n.</em> hill<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/4528.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">ramunong</a></span> [ɾa.ˈmu.noŋ] <em>n.</em> well<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/9236.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">ran</a></span> [ɾan] <em>n.</em> intrinsic character or nature, essence, constititution; basic nature of something resulting from the totality of its properties; often best translated as personality<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/4228.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">rangal</a></span> [ˈɾ·aŋ.·al] <em>vin.</em> wish<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13474.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">räptulì&#8217;fya</a></span> [ɾæp̚.tʊ.ˈlɪʔ.fja] <em>n.</em> coa