om] <em>n.</em> thunder and lightning<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/8296.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">rawn</a></span> [ɾ·awn] <em>vtr.</em> replace, substitute<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/10940.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">rawng</a></span> [ɾawŋ] <em>n.</em> entrance, doorway<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13521.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">rawnlì&#8217;u</a></span> [ɾawn.lɪ.ʔu] <em>n.</em> pronoun<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/5784.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">rawp</a></span> [ɾawp̚] <em>n.</em> bladder polyp<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13617.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">rayl</a></span> [ˈɾajl] <em>adj.</em> feeling pity and sorrow for someone&#8217;s misfortune<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13615.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">räzekx</a></span> [ˈɾæ.zɛk&#8217;] <em>n.</em> curse<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/4480.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">re&#8217;o</a></span> [ˈɾɛ.ʔo] <em>n.</em> head<br 