r /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/10580.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">swoasey</a></span> [ˈswo.a.sɛj] <em>n.</em> kava bowl (constructed from seed pods, used for drinking intoxicating beverages), hand-sized<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/10584.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">swoasey ayll</a></span> [ˈswo.a.sɛj a.ˈjḷ] <em>n.</em> large social kava bowl<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/1932.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">swok</a></span> [swok̚] <em>adj.</em> sacred<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/1936.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">swotu</a></span> [ˈswo.tu] <em>n.</em> sacred place<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13087.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">Swotu Wayä</a></span> [ˈswo.tu ˈwaj.æ] <em>prop.n.</em> sacred place of song<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13086.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">Swotulu</a></span> [ˈswo.tu.lu] <em>prop.n.</em> sacred river<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/4352.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">syä&#