.org/audio/vocab/10432.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">utu</a></span> [ˈu.tu] <em>n.</em> forest canopy<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/10436.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">utumauti</a></span> [ˈu.tu.ma.u.ti] <em>n.</em> banana fruit<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13642.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">uturtu</a></span> [u.ˈtuɾ.tu] <em>n.</em> refugee, person in need of uturu<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13350.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">uturu</a></span> [u.ˈtʊ.ɾu] <em>n.</em> sanctuary, place of refuge<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/2644.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">uvan</a></span> [u.ˈvan] <em>n.</em> game<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/9480.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">uvan letokx</a></span> [u.ˈvan lɛ.ˈtok&#8217;] <em>n.</em> physical or athletic game, sport<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/2648.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">uvan si</a></span> [u.ˈvan ˈs·i] <em>vin.</em> play (a game)</div>
