ight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/3952.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">win säpi</a></span> [ˈwin sæ.ˈp·i] <em>vin.</em> hurry<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/3956.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">win si</a></span> [ˈwin ˈs·i] <em>vin.</em> rush something, make something fast<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/10508.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wìngay</a></span> [w·ɪ.ˈŋaj] <em>vtr.</em> prove<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/2704.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wìntxu</a></span> [w·ɪn.ˈt&#8217;·u] <em>vtr.</em> show<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13429.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">winzaw</a></span> [ˈwin.zaw] <em>n.</em> arrow deer<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13326.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wion</a></span> [ˈwi.on] <em>n.</em> reef<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/9448.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wip</a></span> [wip̚] <em>adj.</em> salty<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/5292.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wiya</a></span> [ˈwi.ja] <em>intj.</em> expression of warning or frustration, &#8220;damn!&#8221;<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/8272.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wo</a></span> [w·o] <em>vtr.</em> reach for<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/5168.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wok</a></span> [wok̚] <em>adj.</em> loud<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/9864.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wokau</a></span> [wok.ˈa.u] <em>n.</em> pendulum drum<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/4700.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wotx</a></span> [wot&#8217;] <em>n.</em> totality, whole<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/5424.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wou</a></span> [ˈw·o.·u] <em>vin.</em> be amazing, fascinating (slang)<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13141.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wrrkä</a></span> [wṛ.ˈk·æ] <em>vin.</em> go out, go outside<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/2716.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wrrpa</a></span> [ˈwṛ.pa] <em>adv., n.</em> outside<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/10404.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wrrza&#8217;u</a></span> [wṛ.ˈz·a.ʔ·u] <em>vin.</em> come out, emerge<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13238.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wrrzärìp</a></span> [wṛ.ˈz·æ.ɾ·ɪp̚] <em>vtr.</em> pull out, extract<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/9272.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wum</a></span> [wʊm] <em>adv.</em> approximately, roughly<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/7516.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wur</a></span> [wuɾ] <em>adj.</em> cool, chilly<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/2720.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wutso</a></span> [ˈwu.t͡so] <em>n.</em> dinner, served meal<br /><span style="font-weight: bold; margin-left: -0.7em;"><a class="map_excluded" href="https://s.learnnavi.org/audio/vocab/13386.mp3" onclick="window.open(this.href,this.target,'width=550px,height=350px');return false">wuwuk</a></span> [ˈwʊ.wʊk̚] <em>n.</em> lizard; any of a variety of lizard-like creatures</div>
